{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 35, :comments ["<b>And at the entrance of the Tent of Meeting you shall sit day and night seven days, and you shall keep the charge of HaShem, so that you do not die</b> — According to the view of the baraita in Torat Kohanim (Sifra, Shemini Millu'im 42), the meaning of this verse is that they shall not go out from the entrance of the Tent of Meeting day and night during the time of the service, that is, until they complete all the service incumbent upon them at that time. And this is a commandment that applies to all generations: a priest may not leave the service and go out, and they are liable to death for it. This is what it says concerning the High Priest (Leviticus 21:12), \"and from the sanctuary he shall not go out and he shall not profane it\" — they said (in Sifra, here): When is it that he does not go out and does not profane? You must say: during the time of the service. And they expounded (there), \"lest you die\" (Leviticus 10:7) — from the implication of the negative you hear the affirmative. I have only Aaron and his sons, who were anointed with the anointing oil, that if they went out during the time of the service they are liable to death. From where do I derive it for all the priests in all the generations? Scripture says, \"for the anointing oil of HaShem is upon you\" (ibid.) — the meaning being that it did not say \"for with the anointing oil of HaShem you are anointed,\" but rather said \"upon you,\" like \"and it shall be to them an anointing, a priesthood forever throughout their generations\" (Exodus 40:15)."], :book :leviticus, :voice :ramban, :lang :en, :chapter 8, :notes {0 "The citation (שמיני מלואים מב) refers to the Sifra's section on Shemini, in the Millu'im chapter, paragraph 42."}, :source-witnesses [{"versionTitle" "Sefaria community Hebrew (PD)", "language" "he"}], :timestamp "2026-07-22T03:52:00.908824958Z", :translated-from :he, :model "glm-5.2"}